WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.839
Next thing that I want you to consider as far

2
00:00:01.839 --> 00:00:03.600
as your passive safety cues, and I think this is

3
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.379
kind of a big 1, is lighting.

4
00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:08.320
The lighting of the space will absolutely have an impact

5
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.699
on your nervous system.

6
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.699
How often do you experience

7
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.219
like a sense of anxiety

8
00:00:13.759 --> 00:00:16.875
when you're in darkness or when maybe there's a corner

9
00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:19.355
of the room you can't see maybe or can't see

10
00:00:19.355 --> 00:00:20.094
very clearly?

11
00:00:21.274 --> 00:00:24.234
And how often do people have difficulty falling asleep when

12
00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.394
it's dark? Even adults, like they have a hard time

13
00:00:26.394 --> 00:00:28.074
falling asleep, they have too much of that flight fight

14
00:00:28.074 --> 00:00:30.800
energy in them. And I think the darkness aspect of

15
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:31.699
it contributes

16
00:00:32.719 --> 00:00:33.620
to those feelings.

17
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.840
Darkness I think in general can trigger defensive feelings and

18
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.659
evolutionarily like there was probably was a reason for that.

19
00:00:41.039 --> 00:00:43.734
If we couldn't see in the dark, we probably felt

20
00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.234
more flight by energy in order to get away from

21
00:00:46.375 --> 00:00:48.155
whatever may be lurking there

22
00:00:48.854 --> 00:00:50.234
or to fight it off.

23
00:00:50.774 --> 00:00:54.134
But I also think that light can be a cue

24
00:00:54.134 --> 00:00:55.909
of danger, or at least too much of

25
00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.289
it. Especially if you're in more of like a shutdown

26
00:00:58.289 --> 00:00:58.789
state,

27
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.810
you may not want a lot of stimulation, and that

28
00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:03.909
may mean you want dimmer lights,

29
00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.390
at least not super bright lights.

30
00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:09.185
Or maybe the quality of a light, like if it's

31
00:01:09.185 --> 00:01:12.224
1 of those flickering fluorescent kind of bulbs, that may

32
00:01:12.224 --> 00:01:12.885
be a

33
00:01:13.344 --> 00:01:14.325
general sense

34
00:01:14.784 --> 00:01:17.204
of danger. Not like you're running away or fighting, but

35
00:01:17.265 --> 00:01:18.405
just a cue of danger.

36
00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.479
I personally in my office here I have a number

37
00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:23.219
of lights.

38
00:01:23.599 --> 00:01:25.299
I have this 1 here in the corner,

39
00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.920
which I can dim if I want to. I have

40
00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.099
this 1 and another 1 that are connected to

41
00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:32.879
to my smartphone, I can dim them if I want

42
00:01:32.879 --> 00:01:35.444
to. I'm actually getting those installed ceiling as well. Those

43
00:01:35.444 --> 00:01:37.204
aren't here yet, but that's the next thing for my

44
00:01:37.204 --> 00:01:38.984
office is to get dimmable

45
00:01:39.284 --> 00:01:40.504
ceiling bulbs

46
00:01:40.805 --> 00:01:42.424
that I can control with my smartphone

47
00:01:42.885 --> 00:01:46.004
to have it just right. I tend to like dimmer

48
00:01:46.004 --> 00:01:46.504
lighting,

49
00:01:46.965 --> 00:01:49.844
especially with like a more of a warm orangey glow

50
00:01:49.844 --> 00:01:53.180
to it, that for my system just feels right, it

51
00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:54.319
feels very calming.

52
00:01:55.819 --> 00:01:58.060
In the daytime though I like to have a lot

53
00:01:58.060 --> 00:01:59.519
of light, I open up my blinds

54
00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:02.719
and let the natural sunlight pour in, that also feels

55
00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:04.995
safe for me. So they both feel safe, it's just

56
00:02:05.155 --> 00:02:08.194
contextually or for what I need in that moment, it's

57
00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.854
just different. If I'm in more of a shutdown immobilized

58
00:02:10.915 --> 00:02:11.415
state,

59
00:02:11.955 --> 00:02:14.835
I want to have less lighting. In the daytime when

60
00:02:14.835 --> 00:02:17.875
I'm more energized and playful, I would I like to

61
00:02:17.875 --> 00:02:20.294
have lots of natural sunlight coming in.

62
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.120
So both scenarios bring a smile on my face or

63
00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.739
bring a a feeling of safety or happiness or lightness,

64
00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:29.659
feelings of ease.

65
00:02:30.519 --> 00:02:32.139
Just contextually, they're different.

66
00:02:33.444 --> 00:02:36.805
At work, I sadly have to deal with white bright

67
00:02:36.805 --> 00:02:37.305
white

68
00:02:37.764 --> 00:02:41.444
fluorescent bulbs that I cannot dim. I can't really turn

69
00:02:41.444 --> 00:02:44.324
them off either. They don't have many lighting options at

70
00:02:44.324 --> 00:02:47.364
all. It's pretty much that or lights off, and you

71
00:02:47.364 --> 00:02:49.020
can't really do therapy with lights off.

72
00:02:49.819 --> 00:02:52.379
So I've added a couple of smaller lamps but it's

73
00:02:52.379 --> 00:02:54.860
still too dim probably for therapy but for me when

74
00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.939
no else is around or when I'm not in session

75
00:02:56.939 --> 00:02:57.520
at least

76
00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.280
I'll turn the awful

77
00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.540
fluorescent 1 off and have my dimmer lights on and

78
00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.164
that really kind of helps me to reduce stimulation

79
00:03:05.944 --> 00:03:08.824
at work and have more of a grounded kind of

80
00:03:08.824 --> 00:03:11.084
sense or feel in my system.

81
00:03:11.944 --> 00:03:15.004
Take a moment right now and just notice the lighting

82
00:03:15.064 --> 00:03:17.004
in your current environment.

83
00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:21.090
Just in your immediate space, what's the lighting like?

84
00:03:21.709 --> 00:03:24.209
And notice within you if you have any

85
00:03:24.509 --> 00:03:26.449
feelings of like or of dislike.

